# text = The Reverend Septimus took off his spectacles , that he might see her face , as he exclaimed returned the old lady Glad to get his spectacles off ( for they always made his eyes water ), her son obeyed : murmuring that his sight for reading manuscript got worse and worse daily his mother went on , reading very perspicuously and precisely Septimus looked at the row of chairs against the wall , with a half - protesting and half-appealing countenance the old lady read on with a little extra emphasis Septimus breathed more freely , and muttered interposed the gentle Minor Canon , laying down his knife and fork to rub his ear in a vexed manner the old lady resumed remarked the Minor Canon in the same tone as before said Septimus , after a little more rubbing of his ear the old lady replied after some hesitation said Septimus .
