# text = From succeeding unconsciousness he passes into a dream of slow uneasiness from cold ; and painfully awakes to a perception of the lanes of light -- really changed , much as he had dreamed -- and Jasper walking among them , beating his hands and feet Durdles cries out , unmeaningly alarmed says Jasper , coming up to him They strike four quarters , and then the great bell strikes cries Durdles , scrambling up As Durdles recalls that touching something in his dream , he looks down on the pavement , and sees the key of the crypt door lying close to where he himself lay he says , picking it up , and recalling that part of his dream .
